# Field TA/DA claims: the FINAL CHECK on the field-expenses dashboard (12 Nov 2026).
#
# After the reporting officer approves a planner month claim it stays
# "Approved" (no payroll yet) and appears on erp.elbrit.org/field-expenses.
# Sathish, the CEO and System Managers check each employee's days there (a
# Claim column next to the worked-out TA / DA), adjust a line with a reason,
# and finalise the WHOLE month with one button: one Additional Salary ("Field
# Expenses Reimbursement") per employee with the final amounts.
#
#   1. Custom fields: Expense Claim Detail -- custom_adjusted,
#      custom_adjusted_amount, custom_adjust_reason, custom_adjusted_by,
#      custom_adjusted_on; Expense Claim -- custom_finalised_by, custom_finalised_on.
#   2. Server Script "Field Expense Claims API" (API, method field_expense_claims).
#   3. "Expense Claim Route": a field claim the officer approves stays Approved
#      (no automatic Verified / Additional Salary any more -- the final check
#      does that). Every other claim is routed as before.
#   4. Web Page "field-expenses": the fx-claims block appended to its script and
#      four small hooks (a Claim column, its cell, a claim row under each
#      employee, render() exposed). RE-RUN THIS CONSOLE after the dashboard is
#      rebuilt / redeployed -- a rebuild replaces the page script.
#
# Paste into ERP > System Console (type Python), logged in as a System Manager.
# 1) DRY = True, "Commit" unticked: only prints.  2) DRY = False, tick Commit,
# then Frappe Cloud -> Clear Cache. Safe to re-run: each step skips what is done.

